+## Advisory namespace and candidate-rank reconciliation — 2026-10-22
+
+Direct source inspection reconciles the namespace conflict that changed the S13 candidate fence allocation:
+
+| Namespace/rank | Existing source evidence | S13 design status |
+|---|---|---|
+| `1` — event chain | `lock_ns()` maps `chain` to 1; the event trigger acquires it through `take_lock()` (`008:1512-1529`). | Preserve as the final advisory rank; source trigger order still needs correction so it is not requested before the lifecycle row lock. |
+| `2` — kill switch | `lock_ns()` maps `killswitch` to 2; `kill_switch()` calls `take_lock('killswitch', ...)` before its OFF-path recovery (`008:1541-1550`, `020:451-462`). | Shared gate for effect-admission paths that inspect switch state; exclusive for the kill-switch transition. The current source has only the exclusive operation, not the proposed common gate. |
+| `3` — hold; `4` — business key | `lock_ns()` maps `hold` to 3 and `key` to 4 (`008:1512-1521`); helpers include hold insertion and business-key acquisition. | Preserve these namespaces and place them after new global-ID locks only after full source-wide conflict ordering is proven. |
+| `5` — sweep | Both `revoke_stale()` and `recover_sweep()` directly acquire `(5, hashtext('sweep:'||t||':'||c))` (`020:9-15`, `020:38-55`). | Reserved for sweep serialization; it cannot be reassigned to the new scope fence. |
+| `6` — global caller IDs | No current namespace-6 source lock was found in migrations 001–026. | Proposed for globally unique `call_id`, `change_id`, and `grant_id` keys; new and unimplemented. |
+| `7` — scope fence | No current namespace-7 source lock was found in migrations 001–026. | Proposed for shared mutation / exclusive recovery scope fencing; new and unimplemented. |
+
+The only directly proven pre-existing cross-namespace edge in this reconciliation is `2 → 5`: `kill_switch()` holds the namespace-2 lock while calling `recover_sweep()`, which acquires namespace 5. Migration 020's public `recover_sweep()` and `revoke_stale()` do not themselves acquire the proposed namespace-2 shared gate. A future additive protocol must therefore define the public recovery entry and a private helper for the kill-switch-held path, so recovery cannot reacquire or upgrade the exclusive switch gate. It must also retain the required `7 → 2 → 5 → 6` order before existing namespaces 3–4, row locks, and chain 1.
+
+This reconciliation confirms namespace allocation and preserves the observed `2 → 5` dependency; it does **not** prove a full pairwise wait graph, direct-DML coverage, effective installed grants, or viability of every later edge in the candidate rank. `lock_ns()` currently recognizes only namespaces 1–4, so any implementation using `take_lock()` for namespaces 5–7 must extend and review that helper or provide a separately specified primitive. Current source has no implemented common scope fence. Keep recovery refused, S13 `NOT_APPROVED`, and lifecycle `NOT_READY` until every granted API/helper/trigger/conflict path and the physical writer barrier are implemented and qualified.
